  "solution": "The logic followed here is:\n\n(1st number + 38) = 2nd number,\n\n(2nd number + 38) = 3rd number.\n\nNow,\n\n(32, 70, 108)\n\n⇒ (32 + 38) = 70,\n\n⇒ (70 + 38) = 108.\n\nNow, checking the options:\n\nOption 1: (44, 82, 124)\n\n⇒ (44 + 38) = 82,\n\n⇒ (82 + 38) = 120 ≠ 124,\n\nOption 2: (34, 62, 112)\n\n⇒ (34 + 38) = 72 ≠ 62,\n\n⇒ (62 + 38) = 100 ≠ 112.\n\nOption 3: **(42, 80, 118) **\n\n**⇒ (42 + 38) = 80,**\n\n**⇒ (80 + 38) = 118 = 118.**\n\nOption 4: (38, 76, 116)\n\n⇒ (38 + 38) = 76,\n\n⇒ (76 + 38) = 114 ≠ 116.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option 3\".",
